                    <statement>
                       <p>Write a function called <c>cur_stud_link(soup)</c> that uses the passed soup object to return the URL that links to Current Students in the Navigation Bar.
                        The soup object is created from the file <c>UMich-8-16-2026.html</c> which is a saved version of <q>https://umich.edu/</q> from 2026. 
                        Click on the following link to view the source:<url href="http://web.archive.org/web/20260808043645/https://umich.edu/">link</url>.

                        For example, <c>cur_stud_link(soup)</c> should return <c>'https://umich.edu/web/20260808043645/https://umich.edu/current-students/'</c>.
                        </p>

    </statement><program interactive="activecode" language="python3" add-files='umich-id'>
        <code>
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
import requests

def cur_stud_link(soup):


# read the saved file
fh = open('UMich-8-16-2026.html')
text = fh.read()
fh.close()

# create the soup object and print the results
soup = BeautifulSoup(text, 'html.parser')
print(cur_stud_link(soup))
====
import unittest
import requests
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

class myTests(unittest.TestCase):

    def testOne(self):
        fh = open('UMich-8-16-2026.html')         
        text = fh.read()
        fh.close()
        soup = BeautifulSoup(text, 'html.parser')
        self.assertEqual(cur_stud_link(soup), 'https://umich.edu/web/20260808043645/https://umich.edu/current-students/')

unittest.main()
        </code>
    </program>
</activity>


